   "spoken": "A key idea against b4: don't reflexively move the attacked knight — capture on e6 and counter-attack, or even leave the knight and play the knight to d4, meaning to crash on c6, hitting the queen and pawn for a huge attack. That is compensation — a lasting advantage in return for the piece.",
