   "line": [],
   "spoken": "Time for a key concept — undefended pieces. A type-one undefended piece is defended by nothing at all; here that is the pinned rook. A type-two undefended piece is defended by only one other piece, and pawns do not count.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 46,
   "t": 1442.5,
   "fen": "b2r2k1/p2n1R1p/1prN1np1/3p4/8/1P4P1/PB1R1PBP/6K1 w - - 1 24",
   "line": [
    "Rc6"
   ],
   "spoken": "So one knight is type-one undefended, the rook type-two — a desperately flimsy structure, the knight defending the rook while itself hanging. Move the knight and the rook falls; move the rook and the knight falls.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 48,
   "t": 1453.5,
   "fen": "b2r4/p2n1k1p/1pr2np1/1N1p4/8/1P4P1/PB1R1PBP/6K1 w - - 0 25",
