   "line": [
    "Rf4"
   ],
   "spoken": "Now, why is White still better even though the worst seems over? Two reasons: Black has a weakness on d5, and specifically an isolated pawn there."
  },
  {
   "ply": 52,
   "t": 1545,
   "fen": "b2r2k1/p6p/1p1r2p1/8/3p1R2/1P4P1/P2R1PBP/6K1 w - - 0 27",
   "line": [
    "d4"
   ],
   "spoken": "And the key question with an isolated pawn — one with no neighbours to guard it — is who controls the square in front of it. Here it is White: Black cannot push, because White takes the bishop and simply wins the pawn."
  },
  {
   "ply": 53,
   "t": 1547.5,
   "fen": "B2r2k1/p6p/1p1r2p1/8/3p1R2/1P4P1/P2R1P1P/6K1 b - - 0 27",
   "line": [
    "Bxa8"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
