   "t": 1550,
   "fen": "r5k1/p6p/1p1r2p1/8/3p1R2/1P4P1/P2R1P1P/6K1 w - - 0 28",
   "line": [
    "Rxa8"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 55,
   "t": 1551,
   "fen": "r5k1/p6p/1p1r2p1/8/3R4/1P4P1/P2R1P1P/6K1 b - - 0 28",
   "line": [
    "Rfxd4"
   ],
   "spoken": "So White blockades the pawn with a rook, tying Black's whole army to its defence — which frees White to expand on the other wing. With a kingside pawn majority, the goal is to manufacture a passed pawn, and best of all a protected one that can never be attacked. Bring the king up carefully — mind that a careless king walk can even be mate — trade down, roll the passer through, and it wins the game."
  },
